<TITLE>Refrigeration Cycle</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>The refrigeration cycle refers to the circulation of refrigerant sealed in pipes through a cycle consisting of components such as the compressor, condenser and evaporator; as the refrigerant circulates through the cycle, it repeatedly changes from gas to liquid to gas, absorbing heat from the cabin and releasing it outside the cabin to provide cooling.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
